  "narrative": "All twelve due estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction. The three context mean-difference tests support the accepted core associations in stringent subsets. H257/R250 tests SMARCA2 dependency after SMARCA4 loss within high-MYC-expression lines and gives +0.799 [0.759, 0.839], a very large signed effect with adequate cell counts (93 exposed, 418 comparator). This is consistent in sign and magnitude with the accepted SMARCA2/SMARCA4 synthetic-lethality-like association, so H257 is accepted and closed. H266/R252 tests the same SMARCA2/SMARCA4 association within adenocarcinoma lines with high ASCL2 expression and gives +0.779 [0.736, 0.822], again large and robust; this supports lineage/transcription-factor context robustness rather than a new main effect. H265/R251 tests the smaller MDM2/CDKN2A association in a stringent high-AXL/high-screen-ROC subset and gives +0.109 [0.039, 0.178]. The interval excludes zero, the estimate is on the same order as the validated core MDM2 effect, and the lower bound is near the practical yardstick. Given that the central MDM2/CDKN2A association was previously validated and many demanding contexts have now supported it, I accept H265 as robustness evidence and close it.\n\nThe nine interaction tests are mostly null for clinically meaningful effect modification. H236/R241, H237/R242, H247/R245, H251/R248, and H252/R249 have tiny point estimates and intervals spanning zero; I reject them as established interactions, not as proof of exact absence of modification. H238/R243 has a small positive signed interaction (+0.028) with CI [-0.015, 0.072], too small and imprecise relative to the huge SMARCA2 main effect, so it is rejected. H249/R246 and H250/R247 are signed opposite to the registered direction or negligible (+/-0.01 to 0.03) with intervals crossing zero; no clinically meaningful effect modification is established, so they are rejected. H239/R244 is the only borderline interaction: WRN/MSI-high by high SLFN11 expression gives +0.061 [0.002, 0.119]. It points in the expected direction and the lower bound is just above zero, but the point estimate represents a small modification relative to the large WRN/MSI main effect, the lower bound is close to no effect, and there is substantial multiplicity with small exposed cells in the interaction cells. I therefore leave H239 unresolved rather than accept a borderline effect-modification claim, and close it because the validation budget is exhausted and I do not want to overinterpret this single borderline test.\n\nFrom a critical-review perspective, these tests use measured predictors and QC variables rather than outcome-derived selection, so direct leakage is not apparent, and all valid cells meet the minimum-size diagnostic. However, marker states and expression categories are observational and correlated with broader genomic instability, mutation burden, lineage, growth rate, and screening context; therefore accepted context results remain associations in this dataset and do not establish causality or generalizability. The null interactions are mostly underpowered or precise enough to exclude only large modification, not all possible modification. The accepted context claims strengthen the robustness of the SMARCA2/SMARCA4 and MDM2/CDKN2A associations, while the interaction panel mostly supports marker-context stability rather than strong biological effect modification. No validation is requested because the voluntary validation budget is exhausted.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 20 appraise update. Accepted robustness refinements: H257 SMARCA2/SMARCA4-loss in high-MYC-expression (+0.799 [0.759,0.839]), H266 SMARCA2/SMARCA4-loss in adenocarcinoma/high-ASCL2 (+0.779 [0.736,0.822]), and H265 MDM2/CDKN2A-loss in high-AXL/high-screen-ROC (+0.109 [0.039,0.178]). These support the accepted core markers rather than new main effects. The active interaction panel is mostly closed as nonmeaningful effect modification: reject H236, H237, H238, H247, H249, H250, H251, H252. H239 WRN/MSI by SLFN11 is borderline (+0.061 [0.002,0.119]); left unresolved and closed because of borderline magnitude, multiplicity, and no validation budget. Validation budget exhausted. Remaining active untested context means are H255 USP7 high MYC, H256 NFE2L2 high MYC, H258 WRN high MYC median, H259 STAT3 high aneuploidy, H260 SMARCA2 high aneuploidy, H261 NFE2L2 high hypoxia, H262 SMARCA2 high hypoxia, H263 STAT3 high hypoxia, H264 MDM2 high hypoxia. Prioritize these high-power context means and accept only if signed interval excludes zero and magnitude is meaningful. Do not make causal or generalizability claims."
